 "description": "The before-and-after visual tour: one screenshot per main screen, one suite on every platform. Run `just e2e macos tour` (or ios/windows/linux/android). Lessons baked in: scroll in increments of 1500 or less (big scrolls time out the host); the schedule drawer stays mounted when closed (wait on field absence, not the drawer); the floating pager covers the table add button after a row lands (scroll before re-adding); a virtualised list unmounts options after scrolling (never click one to close a sheet); toasts and the text caret make pictures differ run-to-run (they are noise, not layout \u2014 the compare tool documents them). On macOS the print preview is a separate native window the driver cannot capture: print shots show the main window. See docs/proof/E2E.md.",
